                &lt;h2&gt;Module 1: Emergency and Security Cordon Fundamentals&lt;/h2&gt;
                &lt;p&gt;This module defines emergency concepts and the purpose of a security cordon at an incident site.&lt;/p&gt;

                &lt;h3&gt;Definition of Emergency&lt;/h3&gt;
                &lt;p&gt;An emergency is a sudden event that threatens life, property, operations, or public order and requires immediate, organized response.&lt;/p&gt;

                &lt;h3&gt;Definition of Security Cordon&lt;/h3&gt;
                &lt;p&gt;A security cordon is a controlled perimeter established around an incident site to isolate risk, protect people, preserve evidence, and support emergency operations.&lt;/p&gt;

                &lt;h3&gt;Why Cordons Are Critical&lt;/h3&gt;
                &lt;ul&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Prevent unauthorized access to hazardous areas.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Protect victims, responders, and the public.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Maintain incident-site integrity for investigation.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Create safe operating space for police, civil defense, and medical teams.&lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;/ul&gt;
            </field>
        </record>

