            <field name="html_content">
                &lt;h2&gt;Module 3: Incident Site Cordon Setup and Zoning&lt;/h2&gt;
                &lt;p&gt;A proper cordon creates order, protects lives, and supports response teams.&lt;/p&gt;

                &lt;h3&gt;Step-by-Step Cordon Setup&lt;/h3&gt;
                &lt;ol&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Initial assessment:&lt;/strong&gt; identify hazard source, blast/fire radius, and movement paths.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Set boundaries:&lt;/strong&gt; establish inner and outer perimeter based on risk level.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Control entry points:&lt;/strong&gt; assign guards and maintain an entry/exit log.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mark and communicate:&lt;/strong&gt; use barriers, tape, signs, and verbal direction.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preserve scene:&lt;/strong&gt; prevent tampering and protect evidence areas.&lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;/ol&gt;

                &lt;h3&gt;Recommended Zone Structure&lt;/h3&gt;
                &lt;ul&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hot Zone (inner cordon):&lt;/strong&gt; immediate danger area, authorized specialists only.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Warm Zone:&lt;/strong&gt; controlled support area for staging and triage access.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cold Zone (outer cordon):&lt;/strong&gt; public separation, media holding, and safe assembly.&lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;/ul&gt;

                &lt;h3&gt;Critical Guard Practices&lt;/h3&gt;
                &lt;ul&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Never leave cordon posts unattended.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Use one communication language and clear commands.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Escalate any breach attempt immediately.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Continuously reassess perimeter as threat conditions change.&lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;/ul&gt;
            </field>
        </record>

