            <field name="html_content">
                &lt;h2&gt;Module 5: Interdepartmental Coordination and General Warnings&lt;/h2&gt;
                &lt;p&gt;Cordon effectiveness depends on synchronized coordination and strict warning compliance.&lt;/p&gt;

                &lt;h3&gt;Departments Related to Crowd/Incident Management&lt;/h3&gt;
                &lt;ul&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineering:&lt;/strong&gt; technology, layouts, flow design, and congestion prevention.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Administrative:&lt;/strong&gt; staffing plans, communication management, operations coordination.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Behavioral:&lt;/strong&gt; psychological and social behavior management of groups.&lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;/ul&gt;

                &lt;h3&gt;General Warnings at Incident Sites&lt;/h3&gt;
                &lt;ul&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Do not allow unauthorized persons to cross any perimeter.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Do not spread unverified information to public or media.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Do not remove or move potential evidence items.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Do not change perimeter boundaries without command approval.&lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;/ul&gt;

                &lt;h3&gt;Post-Incident Improvement Cycle&lt;/h3&gt;
                &lt;ul&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Conduct immediate team debrief after stabilization.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Document weaknesses, breaches, and communication gaps.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Record lessons learned for future event planning.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Collect attendee and stakeholder feedback where practical.&lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;/ul&gt;
            </field>
        </record>

